  "type": "feat",
  "name": "Duelist Finesse (Ex)",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 4th level, a professional duelist gains the benefits of the Weapon Finesse feat with any one-handed gun arm. This ability counts as having the Weapon Finesse feat for purposes of meeting feat prerequisites. In addition, he can select any one-handed gun arm. Once this choice is made, it cannot be changed. Whenever he makes a successful melee attack with the selected gun arm, he adds his Dexterity modifier instead of his Strength modifier to the damage roll. If any effect would prevent the professional duelist from adding his Strength modifier to the damage roll, he does not add his Dexterity modifier. If the professional duelist already has the Weapon Finesse feat, he may take another Combat Feat for which he meets the prerequisites.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
